# Employee Management System in C

## Project Overview
The Employee Management System is a menu-driven console application developed using the C programming language.

It allows users to manage employee information, including employee IDs, names, departments, and salaries.

The project demonstrates how structures and file handling can be used to create a basic record-management application.

## Features
- Add new employee records
- Display all employees
- Search employees by ID
- Update employee information
- Delete employee records
- Calculate annual salary
- Store records using binary file handling

## Technologies Used
- Programming Language: C
- Compiler: GCC
- Storage: Binary File

## Project Structure
```text
08_Employee_Management_System/
│
├── main.c
└── README.md
```

## How to Compile and Run

Compile:

```bash
gcc main.c -o employee
```

Run on Windows:

```bash
employee.exe
```

Run on Linux/macOS:

```bash
./employee
```

## C Concepts Used
1. Structures
2. Functions
3. Pointers and file operations
4. Switch statements
5. Loops
6. Binary file handling
7. Searching and updating records

## Learning Outcomes
This project improves understanding of structured data, file operations, record management, and modular programming in C.

## Future Improvements
- Prevent duplicate employee IDs
- Add employee attendance management
- Generate salary reports
- Add department-wise filtering
- Improve input validation

## Disclaimer
This is an educational project designed to practise C programming concepts. It is not a production-ready HR management system.
